      "message": "test: strengthen the tapscript CHECKMULTISIG asset tests and dump the expected error\n\nThe tapscript/disabled_checkmultisig(verify) failure cases run\nOP_CHECKMULTISIG(VERIFY) on a Schnorr signature. An implementation which\ndoes not disable the opcodes in tapscript still fails them, because a\nSchnorr signature is not a valid DER signature, so these cases cannot\ntell whether the opcodes are disabled. Add a 0-of-0 variant, which\nsucceeds when the opcode is executed, so that only the tapscript rule can\nmake it fail.\n\nAlso write the expected script error of a failure case to the JSON dump\nwhen the spender declares one, and check it in script_assets_test under\nexactly the listed flags. The failure cases could so far only be checked\nfor failing, not for failing for the right reason. Consumers which do not\nknow the new field are unaffected.",
